- The second term \( -9 = N + d_2 \implies d_2 = -9 - N \).

Substituting \( d_2 \) into the 6th term equation:
\[ -17 = N + 5(-9 - N) \implies -17 = N - 45 - 5N \implies -17 = -4N - 45 \implies 4N = -28 \implies N = -7 \]

